# Copy this to CICD_MLops/team1_dnn/.env (or team2_cnn/.env) and fill in your
# dev-tracking values. NEVER commit the actual .env file (it's in .gitignore).
#
# Local development only ever talks to the DEV DagsHub repo. CI talks to BOTH
# the dev repo (to read whichever candidate a team registered) and the prod
# repo (to read the current champion, and — after merge to main — write the
# new one). See CICD_MLops/WIKI/ARCHITECTURE.md §3 and §5 for why.

# ── Local dev (.env) — dev-tracking only ─────────────────────────────────────
MLFLOW_DEV_TRACKING_URI=https://dagshub.com/USERNAME/mlops-dev-tracking.mlflow
MLFLOW_DEV_USERNAME=USERNAME
MLFLOW_DEV_PASSWORD=<your_dagshub_token>

# ── GitHub Actions Secrets (CI only — never put these in a local .env) ──────
# Go to: GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New secret
#
# Secret name                  │ Value
# ─────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MLFLOW_DEV_TRACKING_URI      │ https://dagshub.com/USERNAME/mlops-dev-tracking.mlflow
# MLFLOW_PROD_TRACKING_URI     │ https://dagshub.com/USERNAME/mlops-prod-tracking.mlflow
# MLFLOW_CI_USERNAME           │ USERNAME (same DagsHub account works for both repos)
# MLFLOW_CI_PASSWORD           │ <dagshub token>
# SECRET_TEST_DATA_B64         │ base64 of team1_dnn/secret_test_data.npz (flattened 784 input)
# SECRET_TEST_DATA_B64_TEAM2   │ base64 of team2_cnn/secret_test_data.npz (28x28x1 input — a
#                              │ different shape than Team 1's, hence its own secret)
#                              │ (generate locally with each team's train.py, base64-encode
#                              │  the resulting .npz, paste here — never commit the .npz itself)
#
# Both workflows also set CANDIDATE_ALIAS, ARTIFACT_NAME, SECRET_TEST_PATH as
# plain (non-secret) env values per team — see .github/workflows/*.yml.
